======================================================================
GATE / COMPETITIVE EXAM PERSPECTIVE
======================================================================

49. KEY OBSERVATIONS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Remember:

    Regular Languages
          ↓
        DFA/NFA

    Context-Free Languages
          ↓
        PDA/CFG


Very important:

    DFA < PDA < TM

in terms of computational power for the language classes they can
recognize.

More precisely:

    Regular Languages ⊂ Context-Free Languages ⊂
    Context-Sensitive Languages ⊂ Recursively Enumerable Languages


A classic example separating DFA and PDA:

    {a^n b^n | n >= 0}

is:

    Context-free
    but not regular.


