======================================================================
CHAPTER 13 — COMPLETE SUMMARY
======================================================================

A PDA is:

    Finite Automaton + Stack


The stack provides additional memory.

The stack follows:

    LIFO
    Last In, First Out


Main operations:

    PUSH -> add symbol
    POP  -> remove top symbol


Formal PDA:

    M = (Q, Σ, Γ, δ, q0, Z0, F)


where:

    Q   = states
    Σ   = input alphabet
    Γ   = stack alphabet
    δ   = transition function
    q0  = initial state
    Z0  = initial stack symbol
    F   = final states


Two important acceptance methods:

    1. Final state
    2. Empty stack


Central relationship:

    CFG ⇔ PDA ⇔ Context-Free Languages


Classic PDA language:

    L = {a^n b^n | n >= 0}


Basic strategy:

    Read a's
       ↓
    PUSH
       ↓
    Read b's
       ↓
    POP
       ↓
    Check whether everything matches
       ↓
    ACCEPT


